## Graphite
component-graphite = Graphite
    .genitive = graphite
component-graphite-description-novice = Black-grey and soft; pencil leads are made of it. It conducts current well and hardly reacts with anything — that is why electrodes are made of graphite.
component-graphite-description-school = Graphite is a form of carbon. At a graphite anode it is not the electrode but the solution that is oxidised: a salt solution gives chlorine.
